Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 23:00:40 2026 +0000

    Filter list: one shared copy for the whole site, the CRM asked at most once an hour, and a 429 waited out
    
    The CRM's thread "The filter list is called far more than once an hour" (2026-11-13): GET /api/idx/filters went past the CRM's 30 calls in 10 minutes 24 times from 9 to 13 Nov, 17 of them on 13 Nov, and the CRM then answered 429 for the rest of each 10 minutes ("rate limit ceiling hit, leads being blocked: idx/filters"). Each Cloudflare location and each isolate kept its own copy, and after a failure each tried again 2 minutes later.
    
    idx-lib/catalog.js:
    - One copy for every visitor everywhere, in the site's R2 bucket (cache/filters.json). The CRM is called only when it is missing or over an hour old, and only by the caller that wins a compare-and-swap lock (cache/filters.lock, good for 2 minutes).
    - On a 429 or 503 the last good copy keeps being served, and nobody calls until the CRM's retry-after has passed; any other failure waits 2 minutes. Never retried at once, never from the edge cache.
    - Each isolate reads the bucket at most once a minute. In the first moments after a deploy, a caller that loses the lock reads the winner's copy 1.5 s later.
    
    tools/idx-test.mjs: 100 isolates make one CRM call; after a 429 all serve the last copy, one try is made and none until retry-after passes (fails with the lock removed).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
